-- `States`, the theorem-like items, and every clause group.


-- `States` defines a named statement with a `that:` body. The `States:` section
-- itself takes no argument; prose describing it goes in `Documented:`.
[\commutes:with{y}]
States:
when: y is \element:of{\unit.set}
that:
. forAll: x is \element:of{\unit.set}
  then: x "in" \unit.set
Documented:
. called: "commutes with $y?$"
. description: "Order does not matter."
Id: "bc970e75-9dfb-4274-b470-6fa57ea77741"


-- Theorem-like items share one shape: `then:` is required, and `given:`,
-- `where:` and `iff:` are optional. Without a heading, the item is anonymous.
Theorem:
given:
. A is \set
. B is \set
where: A \:subset:/ B
then: A \:subset?:/ B
Documented:
. called: "a subset is a subset"
Id: "1706b3ba-b789-448c-a5c4-d2bc619e1933"


-- With a heading, the result registers a command and can be referenced.
[\membership.axiom]
Axiom:
given: X is \set
then: X is? \set
Documented:
. called: "the membership axiom"
Id: "d570056b-6eb9-41fb-8284-4adbe6ddeda8"


[\open.question]
Conjecture:
given: n is \natural
then: n is? \natural
Documented:
. called: "an open question"
Id: "e6d5caf7-f4bf-4333-8e6f-b3c65d38cfb2"


-- `iff:` states the converse alongside `then:`.
Theorem:
given: n is \natural
then: n is? \natural
iff: n is? \natural
Documented:
. called: "a trivial equivalence"
Id: "862537de-6ab3-4b30-b4e9-2651927ab166"


-- Every clause group, in one place.
Theorem:
given: n is \natural
then:
. allOf:
  . n = n
  . anyOf:
    . n = n
    . oneOf:
      . n = n
      . not: n = n
. forAll: m is \natural
  where: m = m
  then: m = m
. exists: m is \natural
  suchThat: m = m
. existsUnique: m is \natural
  suchThat: m = m
. if: n = n
  then: n = n
. let: m := n
  then: m = m
. given: m is \natural
  then: m = m
. equivalently:
  . n = n
  . n = n
. piecewise:
  if: n = n
  then: n = n
  else: n = n
. have: n = n
  iff: n = n
Documented:
. called: "every clause group"
Id: "85a7e92b-f346-4d3c-b618-b64c9b683d71"


-- A `have:`/`asserting:` group is the escape hatch: it asserts the `have:`
-- items hold given the `asserting:` items. `because:` and `by:` record
-- justification the checker only reference-checks.
Theorem:
given: n is \natural
then:
. have: n = n
  asserting: n = n
  because: n = n
  by: \membership.axiom
Documented:
. called: "an asserted step"
Id: "9539b3b1-6b22-4a24-8fd2-84f87f9f8f5d"
